{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397964,"nonce":"l3E2BZm+PSYdQaPvRETNZQwSby4=","title":"LSP completion is not scope- or type-aware","message":"Measured 2026-10-19 by driving `rayzor lsp` (HEAD a5153c9c) over stdio with a scripted client on a 10-line Main.hx.\n- Completion returned 654 items: every keyword plus every exported symbol in the whole symbol table (`analysis::collect_completions`, `lsp/src/analysis.rs:409`). The file's own locals (`total`), its own static method (`add`) and `trace` were missing. User-file symbols are only included when their file id is 0 and their location is valid, so 72a3386418f58994afbee5392e994214cc2a8acf9db84f5bb8c60e19186dc48a hides them.\n- Typing `total.` returned the same 654 items: there is no member completion. The `.` and `:` trigger characters are advertised, but the position is ignored (`LspContext::completions` takes `_uri` only).\n\nNeeded:\n- locals and parameters in scope at the cursor;\n- members of the receiver's type after `.`, including static vs instance, `using` extensions and abstract `@:forward` fields;\n- types after `:` and `new`;\n- import paths;\n- enum constructors in `case`;\n- override and metadata completion.","files":null}]}